__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.env
.DS_Store

# Intermediate JSON from `--debug`. Sanitized, but still a per-run artefact that
# has no business in the history.
debug/

# The database is NOT committed, as of 2026-10-04. It used to be: it is how
# deduplication and the "already parsed" flag survive between runs, which is a
# real thing to give up, and the trade is deliberate. This repository is public
# and the database holds raw newsletter HTML fetched from a personal mailbox,
# including per-subscriber tracking tokens in the stored URLs -- about 1.3 MB of
# it on the day this changed, because `prune` only empties bodies older than
# `email_body_retention_days`.
#
# What this costs, so it is not a surprise later:
#   * A scheduled Actions run starts with no state, so it re-fetches, re-parses,
#     re-classifies and re-enriches the whole window every time. On a free LLM
#     tier that is the cost that runs out.
#   * Cross-run deduplication is gone, so one article arriving in two weeks of
#     mail can appear in two digests.
#   * `.github/workflows/weekly.yml` still names `data` in its commit step. It
#     now adds nothing there, which is harmless but misleading.
#
# To keep the incremental behaviour without publishing the mail, cache the file
# in Actions (actions/cache on data/news.db) instead of committing it.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db.bak

# Real newsletter fixtures. They carry the mailbox address in their Received
# headers and, for some publishers, a per-subscriber id inside every link
# (Piano's `/-c/117/.../20018313/860429/...` segment is constant across an
# issue). Committing one publishes both. Keep them locally -- they are what the
# extractor is developed against -- and let the two synthetic fixtures below,
# which are hand-written and carry nothing real, be the ones the tests assert on.
# The safe default is ignored, so a newly dropped-in real issue is never
# committed by accident. A SYNTHETIC fixture has to be listed below to be
# tracked -- and the tests import it by name, so a missing line shows up as a
# failing test rather than as silence.
tests/fixtures/emails/*.eml
!tests/fixtures/emails/guardian_saturday.eml
!tests/fixtures/emails/elpais_semana.eml
!tests/fixtures/emails/tracked_newsletter.eml
